# a message/rfc822 part with a content-disposition: the mime
# fields of that part should include the content-disposition
depends empty-inbox
send 24
a append INBOX () {519+}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
To: info@example.com
Subject: Fw: the original
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=b

--b
Content-Type: text/plain

Please find attached the complete message.
--b
Content-Type: message/rfc822
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=original.eml

From: info@example.com
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
Subject: the original
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200

Anything at all.
--b--

receive 4
* 1 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
a OK [APPENDUID 1 1] done
send 1
b fetch 1 (body.peek[2.mime])
receive 6
* 1 FETCH (BODY[2.MIME] {88}
Content-Type: message/rfc822
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=original.eml

)
b OK done
end
